# Git and changelog

## Changelog (`CHANGELOG.md`)

Write **simple English**, one line per change, newest first.

Use a label, then a short fact:

- `Bugfix - Parser was broken; valid in-game codes failed the checksum`
- `Feature - Import several share codes one after another`
- `Change - Import no longer stops at 10 boards`
- `Docs - Added evyx.gg to the resource list`

Put work that is not in a tagged release under `## Unreleased`. Move those lines into the version section when a `v*` tag goes out.

Do **not** paste full commit messages into the changelog.

## Code commits

Keep commit messages **detailed**. Explain why the change exists, not only what files moved.

Good: the body can be several sentences (decoder table, folder limits, CI, and so on).
Bad: only `fix parser` with no context.

The changelog line and the commit message are different on purpose: glanceable vs. complete.
